---
/**
 * NgoSiteHeader — the NGO masthead. A floating translucent "glass" pill, the SAME chrome as
 * Consultancy's SiteHeader, confirmed against `7429:5891` and re-checked against all four
 * sibling NGO frames (Home 7417:7718, About-alt 7434:8916, Program 7447:6222, Contact
 * 7461:6062) — every one is identical:
 *   - wrapper `Background` 1440×102, `fills: []` (no fill at all), padding 16/32/0;
 *   - the bar itself 1376×86, `cornerRadius: 16`, fill `#FFFFFF` at 85%, BACKGROUND_BLUR 6.
 *   Height reconciles as 16 + 54 (tallest child: the buttons) + 16 = 86.
 *   This component previously described the masthead as a solid full-bleed white bar with no
 *   radius, translucency or blur. That was a misread: the 1440×102 measurement belongs to the
 *   *wrapper*, which is unfilled, and the fill/radius/blur belong to its 1376-wide child.
 *   It stays a separate component from SiteHeader only because the nav model differs (no
 *   dropdowns, no carets, different cell metrics) — not because the chrome differs.
 *   - nav → NGO · About us · Programs · Resources · Contact (see `ngoPrimaryNav`), Arial 700/18,
 *     in cells carrying a `minWidth` of 90.64 (see the CSS note — the uneven gaps are real).
 *   - actions → 24px search glyph + two `GIEVA Button`s: "Donate" (secondary: green fill 5% /
 *     border 10% / green label) and "Get Involved" (primary: solid green / white label).
 * The FOOTER, by contrast, IS the shared component instance in both designs (same
 * "oo-footer → Footer"), so NGO reuses SiteFooter themed via [data-brand='ngo'] tokens.
 *
 * NOT done here, deliberately: in every frame this pill is drawn *over* the hero
 * (`Background.y === Main.y`, `scrollBehavior: FIXED`) rather than sitting above it in flow.
 * That is the shell-level gap recorded in docs/consultancy-build-plan.md for all 18 routes, and
 * it can't be fixed in the header alone — each page's hero top spacing was authored to clear an
 * in-flow header, so overlaying without re-deriving those paddings moves every hero *up* by a
 * header height. It belongs to the per-page passes.
 *
 * Zero-JS baseline (WORKFLOW.md §1.5): every link/control is a real, keyboard-reachable
 * element. No NGO mobile frame exists in the design, so the mobile collapse is a native
 * <details>/<summary> disclosure (works with no script), mirroring SiteHeader. Desktop and
 * disclosure copies of the nav/actions are duplicated but only one is ever in the a11y tree at
 * a time. Active state uses aria-current="page" (native), not a visual-only cue.
 *
 * Between 1440 and the disclosure the layout follows a three-tier FIT LADDER — see the @media
 * block at the foot of the stylesheet. The design authorises exactly one width, so the ladder is
 * ours; what it replaces is a `flex-wrap: wrap` that broke the five nav labels across three rows
 * on any viewport under 1420px, 1366px laptops included.
 */
import { ngoPrimaryNav, isActive } from '@lib/nav';
import Button from '@components/Button.astro';
import SiteSearch from '@components/SiteSearch.astro';
import BrandLockup from '@components/BrandLockup.astro';

const current = Astro.url.pathname;
---

<header class="ngo-header">
  <div class="ngo-header__bar">
    <BrandLockup href="/ngo" ink="brand" destination="NGO home page" />

    <nav class="ngo-nav ngo-nav--desktop" aria-label="Primary" data-search-anchor>
      <ul role="list" class="ngo-nav__list">
        {
          ngoPrimaryNav.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <a
                class="ngo-nav__link"
                href={item.href}
                aria-current={isActive(current, item.href) ? 'page' : undefined}
              >
                {item.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="ngo-header__actions ngo-header__actions--desktop">
      <SiteSearch iconSize={24} />
      <Button variant="secondary" href="/ngo/donate">Donate</Button>
      <Button variant="primary" href="/ngo/get-involved">Get Involved</Button>
    </div>

    <details class="ngo-header__menu">
      <summary class="ngo-header__menu-toggle">
        <span class="visually-hidden">Open menu</span>
        {
          /* `menu-02` — the same glyph SiteHeader now carries. NGO has no mobile frame of its
             own; the two mastheads have always drawn the identical toggle, so it takes the
             Consultancy frame's confirmed icon rather than keeping the even 3-bar we drew. */
        }
        <svg
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          aria-hidden="true"
          focusable="false"
        >
          <path
            d="M4 5H16M4 12H20M4 19H12"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.25"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
        </svg>
      </summary>

      <div class="ngo-header__menu-panel">
        <nav class="ngo-nav" aria-label="Primary">
          <ul role="list" class="ngo-nav__list">
            {
              ngoPrimaryNav.map((item) => (
                <li>
                  <a
                    class="ngo-nav__link"
                    href={item.href}
                    aria-current={isActive(current, item.href) ? 'page' : undefined}
                  >
                    {item.label}
                  </a>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </nav>
        <div class="ngo-header__actions">
          <Button variant="secondary" href="/ngo/donate">Donate</Button>
          <Button variant="primary" href="/ngo/get-involved">Get Involved</Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</header>

<style>
  .ngo-header {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 50;
    /* Wrapper `Background` 7429:5890: 1440×102, unfilled, padding 16/32/0. No bottom border —
       the design draws none, and a hairline would defeat the point of a floating pill. */
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--shell-gutter) 0;

    /* ── Fit ladder (see the @media block at the foot of this file) ──────────────
       The design fixes one width, 1440. Every narrower desktop width is ours to author, and
       the four values below are the only dials the ladder turns. Tier A is design-exact. */
    --shell-gutter: var(--space-lg); /* 32 — the wrapper's horizontal padding */
    --bar-pad-inline: var(--space-lg); /* 32 — the pill's own padding */
    --bar-gap: var(
      --space-md
    ); /* MINIMUM gap between the three groups, not the rendered one */
    --nav-gap: var(--space-md); /* 24 — itemSpacing on 7429:5893 */
    --nav-cell-min: 90.64px; /* the design's per-cell minWidth (see the cell rule below) */
  }
  .ngo-header__bar {
    position: relative;
    /* 1376 — inset 32px from the frame, wider than the 1312 content column. */
    max-width: var(--shell-max);
    margin-inline: auto;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    /* `space-between` distributes the slack, so `gap` only ever acts as a floor — at 1440 the
       rendered gaps are ~37px either way. Declaring the floor at 24 rather than 32 therefore
       costs nothing at the design width and buys 16px of headroom before the pill runs out of
       room, which is 16px of Tier A we get for free. */
    gap: var(--bar-gap);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--bar-pad-inline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.85);
    backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
  }
  /* Safari < 18 needs the prefixed property, and it must sit in its own block — Lightning CSS
     collapses a prefixed/standard pair in one block down to the prefixed form alone, which
     drops the blur in Chrome and Firefox. (Same treatment as SiteHeader.) */
  @supports (-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) {
    .ngo-header__bar {
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
    }
  }
  /* Lockup styling — including its `flex: none` — lives entirely in BrandLockup.astro; the NGO
     header instances the same 247×48 lockup as Consultancy and the footer. */

  /* The desktop nav neither wraps nor shrinks: it is a rigid block whose width the fit ladder
     steps down deliberately. It used to be `flex-wrap: wrap`, which made it the only thing in
     the pill that could give (the lockup and the actions are both `flex: none`) — so below
     1420px it broke the five labels across two and three rows and grew the pill from 86px to
     120px. Wrapping is never a correct outcome for a masthead; running out of room is a
     breakpoint's job, not a line-break's. */
  .ngo-nav--desktop {
    flex: none;
  }
  .ngo-nav__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--nav-gap);
  }
  /* Each nav cell carries `minWidth: 90.64` with its label centred inside (7429:5891 →
     7429:5894 et al). That, not the 24px gap alone, is what produces the design's uneven-looking
     label spacing — 54/33/27/35px between words rather than a flat rhythm. 90.64 is not a
     design-system step; it is residue from whatever label was once widest. Reproduced verbatim
     because all five NGO frames agree on it, and exact-replica comes first. Desktop only: the
     mobile disclosure stacks its links full-width.
     It is also 92px of pure optical padding around a nav whose labels only need 458px, which is
     why Tier B is able to give it up first: it is the one nav value that buys nothing but the
     design's rhythm, and the design's rhythm is only specified at 1440. */
  .ngo-nav--desktop .ngo-nav__list > li {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    min-inline-size: var(--nav-cell-min);
  }
  .ngo-nav__link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--color-text-default); /* #120633, the variable-bound nav ink */
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: var(--type-body-lg-size);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); /* design nav labels are Arial 700 */
    line-height: var(--type-body-lg-line);
    padding-block: var(--space-3xs);
  }
  .ngo-nav__link:hover {
    color: var(--color-cta);
  }
  /* Inferred: no NGO frame shows an active nav item. Colour alone now carries it — the labels
     are all bold at rest, so the weight it used to add is no longer a distinguishing cue. */
  .ngo-nav__link[aria-current='page'] {
    color: var(--color-cta);
  }

  .ngo-header__actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    flex: none;
  }
  .ngo-header__menu {
    display: none;
  }
  .ngo-header__menu-toggle {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    inline-size: 2.5rem;
    block-size: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text-default);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .ngo-header__menu-toggle::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .ngo-header__menu[open] .ngo-header__menu-toggle {
    color: var(--color-action-primary);
  }
  .ngo-header__menu-panel {
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: 0;
    top: calc(100% + var(--space-2xs));
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--color-surface-default);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12);
  }
  .ngo-header__menu-panel .ngo-nav__list {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .ngo-header__menu-panel .ngo-header__actions {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  /* ── Fit ladder ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Authored by us: the design specifies 1440 and nothing else, and there is no NGO mobile
     frame. Each tier's threshold is the measured width at which the tier above stops fitting,
     rounded up for headroom; `npm run verify:local` pins them (tests/header-fit.spec.ts).

       ≥1420  A — design-exact. 90.64 cells, 24px nav gap, 32px pill padding and page gutter.
                  (measured floor 1414, 6px headroom — deliberately the tightest of the three:
                  every pixel below 1420 that stays in Tier A is a pixel of design fidelity.)
       ≥1340  B — cells hug their labels. The only thing lost is the design's 1440-only optical
                  rhythm; label sizes, weights and the 24px gap are untouched. (floor 1321)
       ≥1260  C — our own slack comes off: page gutter and nav gap halve, pill padding drops to
                  24. Design values, but no longer the design's values — legible over exact.
                  (floor 1241)
       <1260  the disclosure. Previously 900px, which was ~520px below the width at which the
              desktop layout actually stopped fitting; that gap is what the wrap lived in.

     Nothing here fires at 1440, so parity with 7429:5891 is untouched. */
  @media (max-width: 1419.98px) {
    .ngo-header {
      --nav-cell-min: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 1339.98px) {
    .ngo-header {
      --shell-gutter: var(--space-sm);
      --bar-pad-inline: var(--space-md);
      --nav-gap: var(--space-sm);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 1259.98px) {
    .ngo-nav--desktop,
    .ngo-header__actions--desktop {
      display: none;
    }
    .ngo-header__menu {
      display: block;
    }
  }

  /* ── Mobile bar ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Mirrors SiteHeader's — see the note there. The flat, full-bleed 64px treatment is read off
     the CONSULTANCY mobile frame (12490:11659); NGO has no mobile frame yet. Applied here on
     the same grounds as the toggle glyph above: the two mastheads are the same object in the
     design at every ingested width, so they should not diverge at the one width only one of
     them has been drawn at. */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .ngo-header {
      padding: 0;
    }
    .ngo-header__bar {
      max-width: none;
      border-radius: 0;
      padding: var(--container-gutter);
      gap: var(--space-sm);
    }
  }
</style>
